solutions

KYC/payment prerecorded filler didn’t fire
Fix deterministic routing first. Add exact Hindi/STT variants from the logs:
केवाईसी के बारे, केवाईसी डिटेल्स, मेरी केवाईसी, मेरे केवाईसी, के वैसी, के वाई सी

मेरे पेमेंट्स, पेमेंट्स का बताओ, पेमेंट्स का स्टेटस, पेमेंट्स डिटेल्स

Then add tests using the exact logged utterances. Once these route to kyc.status / payment.summary, the topic filler will fire immediately.

Classifier timed out and route became unknown
Make classifier fallback less fragile.
Best fix: lower max_output_tokens from 1024 to something like 32, because it only returns one enum. Also log response status/error body when _post_responses fails, not just response_received=False.

Latency fix: do not wait the full 10s before filler. If deterministic route is unknown, start neutral filler quickly while classifier runs, then use classifier result for tools when it arrives.

“Main KYC check karti hoon” but no KYC answer
That line should only be said after get_kyc_status actually runs.
Fix prompt/tool logic: after verification succeeds, if there is no post-verification account tool, the model should say “verification complete ho gaya, ab aap kya check karna chahenge?” instead of claiming it is checking KYC.

Better fix: preserve a real pending route only when original route is known. If original route is unknown, don’t pretend we remembered KYC.

After verification, it kept using verify_read_access
This is a code bug in tool selection. For unknown route plus call_verified=True, it should not return only ["verify_read_access"].
Fix: in select_tool_names_for_request, handle call_verified before verified_mobile_last4 for unknown routes. After verified, either allow broad read tools again or reroute the latest user utterance and expose the matching account tool.

Priority order I’d implement: keyword tests/fixes first, then unknown+verified tool selection, then classifier timeout/logging, then TTS proactive reconnect polish.